<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sur Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1540–1556</span> · Also known as Suri Empire, Sur dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sur Empire was an Afghan state founded in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sher-shah-suri">Sher Shah Suri</a>, who drove the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humayun">Humayun</a> out of India in 1540. Sher Shah reformed administration, revenue and coinage, issuing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rupiya">rupiya</a>, and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-trunk-road">Grand Trunk Road</a>. After the death of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> Shah in 1554 the empire split among rival claimants, and Humayun recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in 1555.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sur-empire.jpg" alt="Sur Empire" width="320" height="296" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Map created from DEMIS Mapserver, which are public domain. Koba-chan Borders by Noorullah21 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Sur_Empire_at_its_height.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
